# Backend architecture

Kotlin in this repo is a modular monolith. Read ARCHITECTURE.md §4 (layers),
§5 (no utility code), §15 (what the machine checks) and §18.1 (how tests are
shaped) before inventing a structure. `./gradlew arch` is the command; do not
call Gradle task names by guess and do not wrap them in a second script.

## Where new code goes

A capability is `modules/<name>/{contract,domain,application,infrastructure,web}`.
Neighbours see only `contract`. `domain` depends on `platform:kernel` and
nothing else. `infrastructure` is adapters to the outside world (database,
HTTP, disk) — not use cases and not routes. Only `app` wires implementations.

If the same technical capability would be written twice, it belongs in
`platform/<name>`, not copied into a feature module.

## Ports and names

An interface at a layer boundary is required. There is no `Foo` + `FooImpl`.
The port is named for what the consumer needs (`JobWriter`), not for a
technology. A production adapter lives in `*:infrastructure`, is `internal`,
and is named by mechanism (`PostgresJobs`). It cannot be `Jobs.Postgres`: a
nested type is compiled in the interface's module.

I/O-free production implementations nest on the port: `Jobs.Cached`,
`Jobs.Retrying`. `Jobs.Abstract` only when two adapters share a Template
Method — not on every interface. A test double is a handwritten `JobsFake` in
**`src/test`** of the module that owns the port, never a nested `Jobs.Fake` on
the production type (that class file still ships in the jar) and never MockK
or Mockito (they are banned on the classpath). The same placement holds for
Gradle plugins under `build-logic/`. A new test does not import `io.mockk`.

## What the machine already forbids

Do not restate the Konsist catalogue here. If a shape would fail `./gradlew
arch`, do not write it and then ask for an exception. An
`@ArchitectureException` needs a forty-character reason, an existing ADR, and
counts toward a budget of ten.

Trailing commas stay on multiline parameter and argument lists. ktlint's
profile is `ktlint_official` because `intellij_idea` rejects them.
